[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So about one year ago, I showed you all how you can make your own 3D printable miniaturaturized cities or basically any location online that you were interested in 3D printing utilizing a service called Map to Model. Unfortunately, that service is no longer available. However,'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'today we\'re going to be taking a look at three new products that are going to allow you to create an even cooler versions of these 3D printable miniature cities. Now, the core of this is all a new service that we\'re going to be'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'taking a look at. It\'s called minis skylines.com. This is going to allow us to go in and again select a location, plot out an area, and get that 3D printed. But this new tool has so many more options that are available to it'

[00:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'when it comes to creating these 3D printable maps. It is truly [music] impressive what they have built. And again, it\'s all free. Now, the first thing that you\'re going to do is go to minis skyline.com. And you\'re going to'

[00:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'be greeted by what appears to be a very confusing. There\'s like an overwhelming amount of stuff on screen. Do not be overwhelmed by this. This is just a lot of the different options and toggles and whatnot that are available. The core of'

[01:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this is you can come in and select a location, type in a location, an address, a state, whatever it may be, and it will snap to that and then allow you to then create these 3D printable cities. But what\'s so cool about this'

[01:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one is everything is broken out into color segments and you can control each of the individual segments and how it\'s going to populate. So in this case, this defaulted to Honolulu and as you can see here, here\'s a little cross-section of'

